{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
  "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allyson N. Ho",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The language and structure of the statutory scheme, the tradition of appellate review, and the sound administration of justice all counsel in favor of reviewing EEOC's subpoena enforcement decisions for abuse of discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can you clarify for me exactly what's on appeal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rachel P. Kovner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Historical and functional considerations strongly support an abuse of discretion standard of review here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kovner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KOVNER: Yes. So we think there are two -- two ways. The first has to do with disparate impact, and the second has to do with disparate treatment. May I take the second one first?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why? That's the part I don't understand. I mean, it's -- there's a woman who says, I took a test, physical, and I failed it. Period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kovner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KOVNER: So I think there are two pieces; one is, is it relevant, and the second is, is it an undue burden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kovner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KOVNER: So -- so with respect to the geographic scope, Your Honor, I think it's really important that we didn't initially seek this information with respect to the entire company. We sought information that was limited to information about the test that was complained about at the particular facility in question, in Goodyear, Arizona, where this person was employed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Could you say a little bit, Ms. Kovner, about how it is that you're persuaded that this Court did make a legal determination that was affecting its judgment, as opposed to maybe using some careless words, but was really making a relevancy determination?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm sorry. Why isn't that telling them they can't have that evidence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about the burden on the other party?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Oh, okay. Is the answer just, well, that's constitutional; therefore, it doesn't count, or whatever?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why is that any different here than it is under Rule 401?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's notable here that Congress actually denied abuse-of-discretion review to the district court. It didn't use the Section 10(e) arbitrary and capriciousness abuse of discretion or in-accordance-with-law. It limited the district court's inquiry for subpoena enforcement to whether it was in accordance with law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, Mr. Kinnaird, do you think that your whole argument might be taking the words \"abuse of discretion\" a bit too literally? In other words, your idea is that you can never use that term unless there is some discretion, some real choice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kinnaird (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KINNAIRD: Right. Well, I think if you're looking to institution -- first of all, I think there has to be discretion to be abuse of discretion. I think there has to be. But if you're looking just at a functional analysis of, you know, how you draw the line to cabin the -- the EEOC's discretion, there's no institutional advantage. This appellate court can construe the charge, construe the subpoena, and resolve the legal claims of the potential value of unknown evidence just as well as a district court. These are simply not factual determinations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kinnaird (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Standard review is not going to deter an appeal. It's going to shift the battleground, as it did here, from fights about whether this is discretionary to whether it's an implied use of -- of an erroneous legal concept, and the problem is, is that because relevance is a question of law and not one of discretion, for the appellate courts to be inquiring into whether there was abuse of discretion simply distorts appellate decision making."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ho (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HO: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Let me make one point and then, Justice Sotomayor, respond to your -- your questions. I heard both my friend Mr. Kinnaird and -- and my friend from the government make very categorical absolutist statements about a case -- about cases that involve testing, and the cases that involve testing pedigree information will always be relevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm having a very hard time with your answer. I've never heard of any test that's given that's not in some way job-related."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1248",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cfdf43d41fc84792a7e7ef67dd4a11d2382b831ff5490605ee5faf7e559f31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cfdf43d41fc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. Kinnaird, this Court appointed you to brief and argue this case as an amicus curiae in support of the judgment below."
    },
    {
